{"id":"h15t4","name":"Data Lake Catalog","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["queries"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Implement the catalog of a data lake. Process <code>queries</code> in order (each query is a list of strings, sizes and quotas are written with digits) and return one string per query. Unless written otherwise, a query on an unknown database returns <code>\"false\"</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>[\"CREATE_DB\", db, quota]</code>: creates an empty database with a storage quota. <code>\"true\"</code>, or <code>\"false\"</code> if it already exists.</li>\n<li><code>[\"SET_QUOTA\", db, quota]</code>: changes the quota (it can become lower than the used storage). <code>\"true\"</code>.</li>\n<li><code>[\"ADD_PARTITION\", db, table, partition, size]</code>: adds a partition to a table (a table exists as long as it has at least one partition). Fails with <code>\"false\"</code> if the partition already exists in that table or if the used storage of the database plus <code>size</code> would be greater than the quota. Otherwise returns the remaining storage (<code>quota - used</code>) after the addition.</li>\n<li><code>[\"DROP_PARTITION\", db, table, partition]</code>: removes it and returns its size, or <code>\"false\"</code> if it does not exist.</li>\n<li><code>[\"DROP_TABLE\", db, table]</code>: removes all the partitions of the table and returns how many there were, or <code>\"false\"</code> if the table does not exist.</li>\n<li><code>[\"TABLE_SIZE\", db, table]</code>: the total size of the table, <code>\"0\"</code> if it does not exist.</li>\n<li><code>[\"LARGEST\", db, n]</code>: the <code>n</code> largest tables as <code>\"name(size)\"</code> items joined with <code>\",\"</code>, by size (largest first), then name; <code>\"\"</code> if there is no table.</li>\n<li><code>[\"SNAPSHOT\", db]</code>: saves the current tables and partitions of the database and returns a snapshot id <code>\"db#k\"</code>, where <code>k</code> is 1 for the first snapshot of this database, then 2, and so on.</li>\n<li><code>[\"RESTORE\", db, snapshot_id]</code>: replaces the tables and partitions of the database with the content of that snapshot (the quota is not changed, and a restore can exceed it). Returns the number of partitions after the restore, or <code>\"false\"</code> if the snapshot id was not created for this database. A snapshot stays valid after being restored, and later changes must not modify it.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>queries = [[\"CREATE_DB\", \"sales\", \"100\"], [\"ADD_PARTITION\", \"sales\", \"orders\", \"dt=01\", \"40\"], [\"ADD_PARTITION\", \"sales\", \"orders\", \"dt=02\", \"30\"], [\"ADD_PARTITION\", \"sales\", \"refunds\", \"dt=01\", \"30\"], [\"ADD_PARTITION\", \"sales\", \"refunds\", \"dt=02\", \"1\"], [\"SNAPSHOT\", \"sales\"], [\"DROP_TABLE\", \"sales\", \"orders\"], [\"LARGEST\", \"sales\", \"5\"], [\"RESTORE\", \"sales\", \"sales#1\"], [\"TABLE_SIZE\", \"sales\", \"orders\"], [\"DROP_PARTITION\", \"sales\", \"orders\", \"dt=01\"], [\"RESTORE\", \"sales\", \"sales#1\"], [\"RESTORE\", \"sales\", \"sales#2\"], [\"CREATE_DB\", \"sales\", \"5\"]]</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[\"true\", \"60\", \"30\", \"0\", \"false\", \"sales#1\", \"2\", \"refunds(30)\", \"3\", \"70\", \"40\", \"3\", \"false\", \"false\"]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.array.string queries<br><b>[output]</b> array.string</div>","starter":"def solution(queries):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["système à plusieurs commandes","quotas","instantanés et restauration","copie profonde","tri de sortie"],"minutes":40,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solution(queries)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Ici, la valeur attendue est une liste : compare ce que tu renvoies à « Expected return value » dans les résultats.</li><li>La comparaison est exacte (même type, mêmes valeurs, même ordre dans une liste), sauf les nombres décimaux, comparés à 0,000001 près.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 9 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"queries":[["CREATE_DB","sales","100"],["ADD_PARTITION","sales","orders","dt=01","40"],["ADD_PARTITION","sales","orders","dt=02","30"],["ADD_PARTITION","sales","refunds","dt=01","30"],["ADD_PARTITION","sales","refunds","dt=02","1"],["SNAPSHOT","sales"],["DROP_TABLE","sales","orders"],["LARGEST","sales","5"],["RESTORE","sales","sales#1"],["TABLE_SIZE","sales","orders"],["DROP_PARTITION","sales","orders","dt=01"],["RESTORE","sales","sales#1"],["RESTORE","sales","sales#2"],["CREATE_DB","sales","5"]]},"expected":{"value":["true","60","30","0","false","sales#1","2","refunds(30)","3","70","40","3","false","false"]}},{"input":{"queries":[["ADD_PARTITION","x","t","p","1"],["CREATE_DB","x","10"],["CREATE_DB","y","10"],["ADD_PARTITION","x","b","p1","5"],["ADD_PARTITION","x","a","p1","5"],["LARGEST","x","1"],["SNAPSHOT","y"],["RESTORE","x","y#1"],["SET_QUOTA","x","4"],["ADD_PARTITION","x","a","p2","0"],["DROP_PARTITION","x","a","p1"],["DROP_PARTITION","x","a","p1"],["TABLE_SIZE","x","a"],["LARGEST","x","5"],["DROP_TABLE","x","a"]]},"expected":{"value":["false","true","true","5","0","a(5)","y#1","false","true","false","5","false","0","b(5)","false"]}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":""}